{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MxF66YZyyksyVrergFgaxY","type":"tool_result","content":"# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D26 seen, D27+ forecast)\n\nScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\nGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 25 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\nTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\nin `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\nreflection) on D1-D19. D15\nadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\nMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\nlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\nD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\nD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\nkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\ngenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\nclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\nD20 (Loaded Later, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\"; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary DEX and recover\nthe module contract\"): 7-entry APK with `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain dex 035); NEW codec `dynamic` whose `data` is\nthe ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\nin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\nD21 (Debug Me If You Can, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\"; prompt \"Neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine\nwhile retaining the intended app flow\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse` (d2/d8) -- the D20 pointer did\nNOT persist. First manifest with `android:debuggable=\"true\"` (single/TT/Mastery-d21 only). No debugger/TracerPid/clock\nAPI and no state loop in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nD22 (Root of Trust, `root_detection` \"synthetic root detection\"; prompt \"Model and bypass multiple synthetic root signals\nwithout globally patching success\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec `base64` (4th time), debuggable false again. No root\nprobe API (File/Build/Runtime.exec/su/magisk) in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `rootSignals` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nFIRST 6-set Mastery (d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22 base64).\nD23 (Hook Line and Signal, `hook_detection` \"hook and instrumentation detection\"; prompt \"Separate real instrumentation\nsignals from generated false positives\"): single = v1 `xor` (key 81). **TT and all 7 Mastery sets (d02, d06, d10, d14,\nd15, d22, d23 -- old days REGENERATED) shipped puzzle schema v2 `{\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..}` with NO data: the answer\nis COMPUTED by dex code** -- `Release.code(Context)` = `\"ANS-\"` + 16 hex nibbles of a static 64-bit mixer chain\n(`token()` = mixA(scanB(mixC(seed))); `scan*` folds in `Probe.s1/s2/s3` 12-bit inverse searches and a theme gate fn such\nas `instrumentationSignals = (a^b^c)&7`; d14 set adds an LCG `long[16]` table walk; d15 set calls JNI `nativeShare(long)`\nin `libarena.so`). Unreferenced look-alike mixers/`K*` consts = the \"generated false positives\". Solved by jadx +\njavac-with-Context-stub (LLM worker); the solver had no v2 path and `bytecode_vm_scan` resolved 2 of 8 v2 APKs.\nD24 (Emulator Alibi, `emulator_detection` \"emulator environment detection\"; prompt \"Defeat app-owned environment checks on\nthe same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle\"): single = v1 `split` (`parts[3]` + `order [2,0,1]`). TT + FIRST 8-set\nMastery (d03, d06, d09, d10, d15, d17, d23, d24) all v2 `analysis`, same shape as D23: theme = gate fn\n`EmulatorAlibi.emulatorScore(a,b,c) = (a+b+c)%4` over `Probe.s*` ints, decoys `sealEmu*`/`KQemu*`; NO Build/qemu/sensor/\ntelephony API in any dex. The overnight v2 evaluator (lib deep Dalvik eval + solve.py unicorn JNI hop) solved all three\nmodes first try (single 16.3 s via race probe, TT 2.5 s, Mastery 3.1 s).\nD25 (Integrity Signals, `integrity_signal` \"challenge-owned integrity statement\"; prompt \"Forge or replay a bounded\nchallenge-owned integrity statement and explain the missing binding\" -- Play Integrity nonce/requestHash pun): single =\nv1 `hex`. TT = v2 with gate `IntegritySignals.integrityStatement(long,int) = a ^ (long)b` (first `(JI)J` gate; only 2\nprobe calls), classes `SealCheck`/`VerdictMap`, decoys `KSeal*`/`KStatement*`/`KCert*`; NO PackageManager/signature/\nIntegrityManager/token code. FIRST 9-set Mastery (d01, d04, d07, d10, d14, d16, d19, d22, d25), all v2, and the old-day\nsets now carry their REAL mechanic: d19 set = `Class.forName`/`getDeclaredMethod`/`Method.invoke` dispatch picking 1 of\n8 `Maze.mN(long)` via a packed-switch `dispatch(int)`; d16 set = `native nativeShare(long,int)` with the u16\nlength-narrowing gate in the export. Solver 3/3 first try (single ~5 s race probe,