{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSoFmVrZL1jbnoX7DE32","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JY1Dor9KGptRcHGPm49WzA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndone=sorted(k.split(':',1)[1] for k,v in st.items() if k.startswith('mobile-android:') and (v.get('ok') or v.get('attempts',0)>=2))\nr=t.index('## Readiness gaps')\na=t.index('Already built or given up',r)\na=t.index('\\n',a)+1\nb=t.index('Forecast after D26',r)\n# wrap list\nwords=[d+',' for d in done]; words[-1]=words[-1][:-1]+'.'\nlines=[];cur=''\nfor w in words:\n    if len(cur)+len(w)+1>118: lines.append(cur.rstrip()); cur=''\n    cur+=w+' '\nlines.append(cur.rstrip())\nbuilt='\\n'.join(lines)+'\\n\\n'\ni=t.index('```json',r); j=t.index('```',i+7)\nold=json.loads(t[i+7:j])\nkeep=[x for x in old if not ('mobile-android:'+x['id'] in st and (st['mobile-android:'+x['id']].get('ok') or st['mobile-android:'+x['id']].get('attempts',0)>=2))]\nprint([x['id'] for x in keep])\nforecast=\"\"\"Forecast after D27: D26's packaging turn did NOT continue -- D27 \"Dependency Surface\" (MASVS-CODE-3 software\ncomposition: \"which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface\") shipped NOTHING real: v1\n`base64` in single + TT, and all 11 Mastery sets went back to v1 with their original codecs (v2 absent after 4 days).\nSo (a) a TT/Mastery regeneration of D27 as v2 or as real bundled-library code is the likeliest near-term mutation\n(priority 1: dependency inventory, exported-surface -> lib-sink reachability, multidex, a `(ZI)I` gate fed by manifest\nfacts); (b) the MASVS-CODE group is now open: CODE-4 input validation (deep-link parse/allowlist bypass, zip slip in a\ndependency, deserialization), CODE-1 platform version gates, CODE-2 forced update (priority 2); (c) still unnamed for\nD28-D31 (4 days): certificate pinning, key attestation, tamper/repackaging, task hijacking/tapjacking, the obfuscation\ncapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and an all-days capstone. Mastery: 11 sets on D27 (+1/day -> ~15 by D31), schema\nper set unpredictable (v1 or v2); keep v1 decoders first in the race, v2 evaluator always armed. Old days not yet seen\nas v2: d05, d08, d12, d18, d20, d27.\n\n\"\"\"\nt=t[:a]+built+forecast+t[t.index('```json',r):]\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"dependency-sbom-inventory\",\"concept\":\"bundled third-party dependency inventory (rows 106-108): library packages outside the app package, versions and their source\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 theme `legacy_dependency` / STRUCTURAL 'reachable challenge-owned dependency' shipped as words only; a regeneration will likely bundle 2+ generated libs. Pure-python `lib.android.dependency_inventory(apk) -> [{pkg, name, version, source, classes, dex}]`: group dex classes by package prefix not under the manifest package (and not android/androidx/kotlin/java), read version from `META-INF/*.version` (androidx style 'x.y.z'), `META-INF/maven/<g>/<a>/pom.properties` (version=), `META-INF/*.kotlin_module`, static final String fields named VERSION/VERSION_NAME/LIB_VERSION in the lib's BuildConfig, `assets/*.jar|*.aar` members (recurse), `lib/<abi>/*.so` version strings (`OpenSSL 1.0.1`, `SQLite 3.x`). Expose as a candidate feature for solve.py: values tied to a lib (ANS- consts, flaw ids like `HCTF-DEP-*`) are tagged with the lib. Regression: synthetic APK with 3 lib packages + pom.properties; D27 fixtures must still return []. Pure python, <0.1 s/APK.\"},\n {\"id\":\"exported-surface-sink-reachability\",\"concept\":\"several generated dependency flaws; only the one reachable from a manifest-EXPORTED component counts (rows 1, 8, 106)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 prompt: 'Prove which generated dependency flaw is reachable from an exported mobile surface'; TT stub `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1`. Build on the existing entry-reachable-callgraph-rank, but start from EVERY exported component: parse the binary manifest for activity/activity-alias/service/receiver/provider with exported=true, or an intent-filter and no exported attr when targetSdk<31 (legacy implicit export), minus those guarded by a signature-level permission; entry methods onCreate/onNewIntent/onStartCommand/onBind/onReceive/query/insert/openFile/call/handleMessage. Walk invoke-static/virtual/direct/interface/super (+ reflection names already resolved by reflection-name-resolve, + Runnable/Handler/Thread.start edges) into lib packages; for each candidate value (ANS- const, flaw id, v2 Release-style chain) record reached/unreached; veto unreached ones in proof_flow ranking. Regression: synthetic APK with 3 libs x 1 flaw each, only one reached from an exported Activity, one from a non-exported Service (decoy), one dead.\"},\n {\"id\":\"v2-boolean-gate-manifest-facts\",\"concept\":\"v2 gate with boolean/narrow args fed by manifest/PackageManager facts (`(ZI)I` exportedReachability; ActivityInfo.exported, permission, targetSdk)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If D27 returns as v2 (TT mutation or Mastery regeneration), the gate is `exportedReachability(boolean z, int i) = z ? i+1 : -1` -- first boolean-typed theme arg. Deep evaluator: correct Z/B/S/C arg + return semantics (if-eqz on Z, int-to-byte/short/char narrowing, boolean returned as int), and intrinsics returning REAL manifest facts: PackageManager.getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_ACTIVITIES|GET_SERVICES|GET_RECEIVERS|GET_PROVIDERS).activities[i].exported/name/permission, getActivityInfo(ComponentName, 0), resolveActivity/queryIntentActivities for the deep link `huntressNN://<slug>/unlock`, ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion/minSdkVersion/flags, ComponentInfo.exported default per targetSdk. Regression: synthetic chain where the boolean comes from ChallengeActivity's exported flag (true) and a decoy non-exported component (false -> -1).\"},\n {\"id\":\"multidex-class-resolution\",\"concept\":\"multidex APK: classes2.dex..classesN.dex, chain spans dexes, duplicate class defs (first dex wins) (row 107)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Every APK so far had one classes.dex; a real dependency surface ships libraries in a secondary dex. Ensure lib.android (puzzle_candidates, deep evaluator, strings scans, proof_flow, callgraph) loads classes.dex, classes2.dex, ... in numeric order (classes10 after classes9, not lexicographic), resolves a class to its FIRST definition (ART/PathClassLoader order), and lets the chain call across dexes (string/type/method ids are per-dex: never share index tables). Also: duplicate class in classes2 with a different ANS- const = decoy. Regression: split a fixture's chain classes across 2 dexes + a shadow copy in classes3.dex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-classfile-jar-dependency\",\"concept\":\"dependency shipped as JVM bytecode (assets/*.jar, .aar -> classes.jar, *.class), not dex (row 108)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure-python class-file reader: magic CAFEBABE, constant pool (Utf8/Integer/Float/Long/Double/Class/String/Fieldref/Methodref/NameAndType/MethodHandle/InvokeDynamic; Long/Double take 2 slots), fields with ConstantValue attribute (static finals), methods' Code attribute; tiny JVM interpreter for static pure methods (iconst/ldc/ldc2_w/lload/lstore/ladd/lsub/lmul/lxor/lor/land/lshl/lshr/lushr/l2i/i2l/invokestatic/ireturn/lreturn/if*/goto/tableswitch) so a v2-style chain into the jar evaluates. Walk nested zips (aar -> classes.jar -> *.class). Regression: synthetic jar with an ANS- const and a 2-method long chain; `javap -c -constants` (installed) for cross-checking while building only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dependency-version-advisory-match\",\"concept\":\"challenge-owned advisory list matched against bundled lib versions (semver, Maven ordering, lexicographic trap) (row 109)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'generated dependency flaw' suggests a generated advisory table (asset JSON or dex string array: id, package, affected range '<1.2.10', '[1.0,1.3)', fixed version) plus several lib versions. Implement version compare: numeric segments (1.2.10 > 1.2.9), Maven qualifiers (alpha<beta<milestone<rc<snapshot<''<sp), '-SNAPSHOT', 'v' prefix, build metadata '+x' ignored; range syntaxes npm/semver (^ ~ < <= >= ||), Maven interval [a,b), python-style '>=1.0,<2.0'. Return affected (lib, advisory) pairs; combine with exported-surface-sink-reachability to choose the one that is affected AND reachable. Regression: table where a lexicographic compare picks the wrong lib.\"},\n {\"id\":\"deeplink-input-validation-eval\",\"concept\":\"exported deep-link handler validates its input (host/path allowlist, startsWith/endsWith/contains, regex, intent:// parseUri) -- the accepted argument feeds the answer (row 112)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"MASVS-CODE-4 is the natural follow-up to D27's 'exported mobile surface'. Model android.net.Uri semantics in the evaluator: Uri.parse never throws; getHost lowercases? (no: returns as given), getPath percent-decoded, getEncodedPath raw, getQueryParameter decodes %XX and '+' -> ' ' only via UrlQuerySanitizer (Uri keeps '+'), returns FIRST duplicate, getQueryParameters all; getLastPathSegment; Intent.parseUri('intent://...#Intent;scheme=..;S.key=val;end'). For validators with a finite accepted set (string equals, startsWith on a const, regex fullmatch with a literal), derive the accepted value and continue the chain with it; record the manifest deep link `huntressNN://<slug>/unlock` as the default input. Regression: synthetic handler where `host.endsWith(\\\"huntress.local\\\")` is bypassable and the chain mixes the accepted host.\"},\n {\"id\":\"zip-slip-entry-normalize\",\"concept\":\"archive extraction in a dependency: entries with ../, absolute, backslash or duplicate names; only the entry that resolves to the checked path counts (row 110)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Classic vulnerable-dependency flaw (zip slip, CVE-2018 class). When an APK asset is a zip/jar that the dex extracts (ZipInputStream.getNextEntry + new File(dir, name) + FileOutputStream, or a lib unzip helper), resolve each entry like Java: File(dir,name) concatenation, getCanonicalPath() normalisation of '..' and '.', backslash kept as a literal char on Android, absolute names re-rooted under dir by File(parent, child), later duplicate entries overwrite earlier ones; then answer the dex's read of the target path (e.g. files/config.json or the code-cache dex). Use raw central-directory names (zipfile sanitises) -- read via the existing zip-structure-anomaly-scan parser. Regression: synthetic asset zip with 3 entries resolving to the same path.\"},\n {\"id\":\"sdk-int-platform-gate\",\"concept\":\"branches on Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion (legacy platform behaviour, implicit export pre-31) (row 111)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'legacy_dependency' hints at legacy-platform behaviour too (MASVS-CODE-1). Evaluator intrinsics: Build.VERSION.SDK_INT / RELEASE / CODENAME from the pinned-emulator profile (keep the value in ONE place with pinned-emulator-env-profile; default API 34, RELEASE '14'), ApplicationInfo.targetSdkVersion / minSdkVersion from the APK's own <uses-sdk> (binary manifest), Build.VERSION_CODES constants inlined by javac (sget vs const). Exported default: android:exported absent + intent-filter -> exported iff targetSdk < 31. Regression: a chain that takes a different branch at targetSdk 30 vs 31.\"},\n {\"id\":\"app-update-version-gate\",\"concept\":\"forced-update / minimum-version gate: PackageInfo.versionCode/versionName compared with an asset or dex minimum (MASVS-CODE-2) (row 109)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Supply